! ML fracture-surrogate regression test: katdiss reference deck run.1 (ver1.2
! database, cement-in-domain, RegI inlet) shortened to 300 y, with the
! FRACTURE_ML_SURROGATE block active on the fracture material (ID 3).  The
! REGRESSION block records the surrogate-owned porosity and permeability of
! fracture cells 91..116 (top z-layer, inlet-most cells first).
! Weight file: bthuber_weights.h5
!==============================================================================
! numo_pr_1d_cement_regI.in — RESOLVED CEMENT LINER deck (QPAC material structure)
!   Grid: 29x1x4 — 3 liner cells (0.025/0.015/0.010 m, R 2.50->2.55) + 26 rock/frac
!   Cement: phi=0.1, k=1.02e-12 m2, QPAC paste inventory + full active set
!   Fracture/rock: v5.2 QPAC-18 mask unchanged
!   Inlet: RegI tunnel water at liner west face (full Z), DIRICHLET head
!     (QPAC SpecifiedHead translation, ~1.64 kPa over outlet; self-limiting)
!   Purpose: Task-1 physical-fidelity case — fracture chemistry EMERGES from
!   paste dissolution (vs prescribed-inlet sweep deck). NOT for the Dakota sweep.
! KNOWN LIMITATIONS:
!   - No porosity-gate yet (POROSITY_RES patch pending): liner cells at the
!     clogging face may VF-creep past physical bounds — watch Portlandite/CSH165
!   - Full-Z inlet face; QPAC's "FracLinerInner" naming may mean fracture-mouth
!     only — one-line region swap if flow field looks wrong
!   - t=0 re-equilibration transient (RegI water vs seeded secondaries)
! Base: v5.2 test deck (below header retained for provenance)
!   aperture 1e-4 m | QPAC RegI inlet | 100 y | obs every step
!   v5.2: pure VOLUME_FRACTION_RATIO area (porosity amplifier removed),
!         rock silicates dissolve-only, ACKNOWLEDGE_ZERO_SURFACE_AREA present.
! Pass: parses; masked stay VF=0; SO4 ~conservative; no C-S-H ladder
!   oscillation; VF bounded. Then: calcite-in-rock check (item c).
!==============================================================================
!==============================================================================
! NUMO Cement-Rock-Fracture Reactive Transport — 2D R-Z  (v4 sweep template)
! numo_pr_1d_v4.template  (from cement_base/v4.in)
!------------------------------------------------------------------------------
! Sources:
!   - Grid/geometry: numo_pr_transport.in (working 2D R-Z deck)
!   - Chemistry setup: pflotran_HDP_3.in (NUMO reference 3D model)
!   - Mineral reduction: March 2026 NUMO report (Section 1.1–1.2)
!   - params.inc: ROCK_APERTURE=1e-2m, CRACK_RADIUS=4.15761m,
!                 FLOW_RATE_FROM_LINER=1e-6m/s, WATER_CHANGE_TIME=5000y
!
! Key corrections vs numo_pr_transport.in:
!   - RATE_CONSTANT in log10 format (no units), matching pflotran_HDP_3.in
!   - SSA values from pflotran_HDP_3.in (10–100 m²/m³, not 1e4 cm²/cm³)
!   - Zero initial VF for seed minerals (not 1e-10)
!   - Quartz_Inert as inert solid filler to close porosity budget
!   - UPDATE_PERMEABILITY disabled (avoids flow NaN from k→0 coupling)
!   - MINIMUM_POROSITY 0.02 (from pflotran_HDP_3.in)
!   - H2O 55.5 T in constraints (not deprecated S type)
!   - MgH2SiO4(aq) commented out (DB typo — missing quote)
!   - ACTIVITY_COEFFICIENTS NEWTON TIMESTEP + NO_BDOT + MOLAL
!   - SNES_TYPE NTRDC (Newton Trust-Region solver fix)
!   - Tracer species for cement-water plume tracking
!   - No INTERPOLATION LINEAR in VARIANT transport condition
!
! Mineral reduction (41 → 29) per March 2026 report:
!   CSH: 10-phase → 3 anchors (CSH165, CSH115, CSH075)
!   C4AH13 removed → C4AH19 retained
!   Hydrotalcite: 4-phase → M4Ac only
!   Katoite: 3-phase → Katoite-Al only
!   Hemicarbonate-Al removed
!
! Throttled rates per March 2026 report (hierarchy preserved):
!   Gypsum:     -2.79 → -6.4
!   Dolomite:   -5.1  → -6.6
!   Calcite:    -5.2  → -6.7
!   Portlandite: -6.0 → -7.0
!==============================================================================

!==============================================================================
! v5 CHANGES (QPAC reaction-mask audit, July 2026):
!   1. FRACTURE MINERAL MASK — QPAC zeroes all AFt/AFm/hydrotalcite/stratlingite
!      /Friedel/gypsum/Portlandite reactions in the Fracture material
!      (Chemistry.inc lines 1013,1160,1616,1801 etc.). Fracture-active in QPAC =
!      C4AH13/19, Calcite, 13 C-S-H, 3 katoites (18). FULL QPAC-18 ACTIVE
!      (March-2026 reduction set aside — preliminary; QPAC set is the
!      reference-validated one). CSH065+CSH055 added to MINERALS/KINETICS.
!      Rock: QPAC allows the same 18 => seeded there too (1e-8, negligible
!      vs rock porosity budget). Mask via constraint: VF=0, SSA=0
!      => zero surface area forever => kinetically inert, but still reported
!      in output (SI observable: "would it have formed?").
!   2. SURFACE_AREA_VOL_FRAC_POWER 0.667 -> 1.0 (QPAC area = SSA*MW = linear
!      in mineral amount; also makes the VF=0 mask permanent).
!      RateScale^2 smoothramp porosity gate (QPAC area itself has NO porosity
!      term; replace 0.8 -> 0 when the POROSITY_RES source patch lands).
!   3. Seeded-mineral SSA rescaled to QPAC-consistent A0 = SSA[m2/g]*rho*VF0
!      so that area(VF) = A0*(VF/VF0)^1 reproduces QPAC's 5.5e7*VF-type slope.
!   4. CSH165 rate -8.44 -> -8.47 (QPAC K_PRIMED); Calcite -5.2 -> -7.50
!      (QPAC RMAX cap = 1 mol/m2/y). C4AH19/Katoite-Al -10.94 already match.
!   5. Rock: QPAC-verified Rock=0 phases (ettringite, hydrotalcites, mono-
!      sulfate/carbonate, stratlingite, Friedel, C4AH13, analcime, brucite)
!      masked with SSA=0. QPAC rock silicates are DISSOLVE-ONLY (min(rate,0));
!      PFLOTRAN has no per-direction flag — left symmetric, see notes.
!   6. Fracture SO4 now has NO sink (as in QPAC): ettringite/gypsum/monosulfate
!      are masked there. Sulfate transits; clogging is C-S-H/carbonate/katoite.
!   7. (v5.2) SURFACE_AREA_FUNCTION switched to VOLUME_FRACTION_RATIO — the
!      POROSITY_ variant's factor is ((1-phi)/(1-phi0))^p (SOLID-fraction ratio,
!      reaction_mineral.F90:2053-2073): in the fracture (phi0=0.99) it AMPLIFIED
!      area ~23x at phi=0.5, ~39x at the 0.02 floor. QPAC area has no porosity
!      term; pure VF ratio is both faithful and removes the amplifier. The
!      porosity shutoff must come from the POROSITY_RES source patch.
!   8. (v5.2) Rock silicates (Albite/Anorthite/K-Feldspar/Muscovite/Phlogopite)
!      set dissolve-only via DISSOLUTION_/PRECIPITATION_RATE_CONSTANT pair,
!      matching QPAC's min(rate,0). Quartz symmetric (QPAC allows both).
!   WARNING: never set VOLUME_FRACTION_EPSILON or SPECIFIC_SURFACE_AREA_EPSILON.
!      For VF0=0 minerals the volfrac-scale branch is skipped and holds a STALE
!      value from the previous mineral (reaction_mineral.F90) — the mask is safe
!      only because area0=0. An epsilon >0 reactivates every masked mineral
!      with a garbage area.
!==============================================================================

SIMULATION
  SIMULATION_TYPE SUBSURFACE
  PROCESS_MODELS
    SUBSURFACE_FLOW flow
      MODE RICHARDS
    END
    SUBSURFACE_TRANSPORT transport
      MODE GIRT
      OPTIONS
        FRACTURE_ML_SURROGATE
          FILENAME ./bthuber_weights.h5
          FRACTURE_MATERIAL_ID 3
        /
      /
    END
  END
END

SUBSURFACE

!==============================================================================
! Regression output: surrogate-owned porosity/permeability of fracture cells
!==============================================================================
REGRESSION
  CELL_IDS
    91
    92
    93
    94
    96
    100
    108
    116
  /
  VARIABLES
    POROSITY
    PERMEABILITY
  /
END

EOS WATER
  DENSITY CONSTANT 1000.d0 kg/m^3
  VISCOSITY CONSTANT 1.d-3 Pa-s
END

!==============================================================================
! Numerical methods
!==============================================================================
NUMERICAL_METHODS FLOW
  NEWTON_SOLVER
    PRECONDITIONER_MATRIX_TYPE AIJ
    RTOL 1.d-8
    ATOL 1.d-8
    STOL 1.d-8
  /
  LINEAR_SOLVER
    SOLVER DIRECT
  /
END

NUMERICAL_METHODS TRANSPORT
  NEWTON_SOLVER
    ITOL_RELATIVE_UPDATE 1.d-5
    ITOL 1.d-8
    RTOL 1.d-8
    MAXIMUM_NUMBER_OF_ITERATIONS 20
    VERBOSE_LOGGING
    !SNES_TYPE NTRDC
  /
  LINEAR_SOLVER
    SOLVER DIRECT
  /
END

!==============================================================================
! Chemistry
!==============================================================================
CHEMISTRY

